{"tool_name":"py-em","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"Py-EM","home":"https://git.embl.de/schorb/pyem","license":"GPL-3.0","summary":"Software tools for automated transmission electron microscopy.","addition_date":"2019-08-09T13:20:47Z","last_update_date":"2020-06-16T10:55:26Z","tool_type":["Library"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:Py-EM","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"pyem-subscribe@embl.de","typeRole":["Primary contact"]}],"documentation":[{"note":"Tutorial material","type":["Training material"],"url":"https://git.embl.de/schorb/pyem/raw/master/pyEM.ipynb?inline=false"},{"type":["General"],"url":"https://git.embl.de/schorb/pyem/blob/master/readme.md"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Microscope image visualisation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3552"},{"term":"Parsing","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_1812"},{"term":"Single particle analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3457"}]}],"maturity":"Mature","name":"Py-EM","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"hans","publication":[{"doi":"10.1038/S41592-019-0396-9","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 2019, Springer Nature America, Inc.The demand for high-throughput data collection in electron microscopy is increasing for applications in structural and cellular biology. Here we present a combination of software tools that enable automated acquisition guided by image analysis for a variety of transmission electron microscopy acquisition schemes. SerialEM controls microscopes and detectors and can trigger automated tasks at multiple positions with high flexibility. Py-EM interfaces with SerialEM to enact specimen-specific image-analysis pipelines that enable feedback microscopy. As example applications, we demonstrate dose reduction in cryo-electron microscopy experiments, fully automated acquisition of every cell in a plastic section and automated targeting o